
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

## Host-side PID calibration simulation

`pid_calibration_sim.py` is a standalone Python model of the relay autotuner in
`src/pid_calibration.cpp`. It needs no toolchain and no hardware:

```
python test/pid_calibration_sim.py
```

It drives the tuner with first-order thermal processes (fast, medium, slow, and
one that never crosses the setpoint), and checks:

- the measured period and amplitude against the simulated process;
- the Ziegler-Nichols formulas for `Ku`, `kp`, `ki` and `kd`;
- that the clamped gains are inside the ranges in `enclosure_pid.h`;
- that the chamber stays below the 50 C abort in the simulated runs.

It is a model of the algorithm, not a compiled copy of it: there is no host C++
toolchain in this development environment. The firmware build covers compilation;
if the model and the C++ ever disagree, the C++ is the source of truth.
